{"EventManager.create destructures destinationCalendar and then unconditionally reads mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration, which throws when destinationCalendar is null/empty, crashing bookings where Google Meet is selected without a Google Calendar destination": 0.8082984685897827, "GoogleCalendarService.updateEvent may pass calendarId=undefined to Google API when externalCalendarId is null/undefined because the fallback .find() compares against the null/undefined externalCalendarId, causing calendar updates to fail": 0.8315545916557312, "organizations/create.handler omits both slug and metadata.requestedSlug when IS_TEAM_BILLING_ENABLED is false, creating organizations with neither identifier, which causes downstream org flows that require one of these fields to throw errors": 0.9076611399650574, "EventManager.createAllCalendarEvents iterates each destinationCalendar entry but passes the full event with the original destinationCalendar array into each calendar service call, causing non-Google calendar services (Office365, Lark) to always use the first destinationCalendar entry, so secondary hosts create events against the wrong calendar or fail": 0.9507153034210205, "EventManager.updateLocation stores booking references using result.externalId/result.credentialId, but CalendarManager.updateEvent never sets those fields in its EventResult, causing editLocation to create new booking references missing credentialId/externalCalendarId and breaking later update/delete operations": 0.9911826848983765, "EventManager.updateAllCalendarEvents can call updateEvent(credential, ...) even when credential is still undefined after DB lookup because Credential.app/appId are optional, causing runtime failures for bookings whose calendar reference points to a credential not present in the in-memory credentials list": 0.956476628780365}